Package: lrmap
Type: Package
Title: Multi-Scale Spatial Co-Location of Ligands and Receptors Between Cell Types
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ruben", "Dries", email = "rdries@bu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: For every sender and receiver cell type and every ligand-receptor pair, measures how
    much ligand from the sender type surrounds receiver cells that express the receptor, at three
    spatial scales: touching cells (contact), short-range neighbours (paracrine) and the regional
    neighbourhood (niche). Significance comes from toroidal shifts of the sender layer against the
    receiver layer, which keep each layer's own spatial pattern. Transcripts leaked between
    touching cells can be estimated and removed (lrmap_leak()).
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports: Matrix, RANN, stats, methods, utils
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), edgeicg, lrmaprs
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
